              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "The finding is classified as a potential undefined behavior risk due to missing null pointer checks for either the source or destination buffer. However, the input does not provide enough context or evidence to confirm that a null pointer dereference is actually possible at this location. Additionally, several key details such as the buffer types, source and destination expressions, and whether any guards or capacity checks are present are missing. As a result, this finding cannot be confirmed as a genuine vulnerability without further manual review and code inspection. The probability of this being a false positive is moderate, as the lack of information prevents a high-confidence assessment.\n\n___\n"
              },
