              "id": "6d90cc29-dd13-4742-b15a-53352943e64c",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a potential undefined behavior risk due to possible overlap between the source and destination buffers in a string copy operation. However, the analysis lacks specific details about the code location, buffer types, source and destination expressions, and other contextual information that would confirm the risk. Without this information, the likelihood of this being a true vulnerability is low, but not zero. Manual review is recommended to confirm whether the source and destination buffers can overlap in this context.\n\n___\n"
