              "id": "d25cb170-72f7-4cad-97e1-4eaa1ca9acac",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination buffers in a string copy operation. When the source and destination memory regions overlap, functions like strncpy can produce unpredictable results, which may lead to data corruption or security vulnerabilities. The classification indicates a high-confidence issue, and there is no evidence in the available context to suggest that the source and destination are guaranteed to be non-overlapping. Therefore, this is considered a genuine vulnerability that should be addressed to prevent undefined behavior.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate the risk of undefined behavior caused by possible overlapping memory regions in a string copy operation, ensure that the source and destination buffers do not overlap before performing the copy. If overlap is possible, use a memory-safe function such as `memmove`, which is designed to handle overlapping regions safely. For example, if you are currently using `strncpy(dst, src, n)`, and there is a possibility that `dst` and `src` may overlap, replace it with `memmove(dst, src, n)`. Always validate that the length parameter does not exceed the size of the destination buffer to prevent buffer overflows.\n\n```cpp\n// Example fix:\nmemmove(dst, src, n); // Safe for overlapping regions\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\n___\n"
