              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as high risk because the destination buffer's capacity is not known, and there is no evidence that the length or count argument used in the buffer operation is proven to be safe. This means there is a significant risk of a buffer overflow if the count exceeds the actual size of the destination buffer. The lack of information about the destination buffer's size and the absence of a proven safe count make this a genuine vulnerability. No mitigating factors such as explicit bounds checks, guards, or evidence that the count is derived from the buffer's capacity are present in the available data.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate this issue, ensure that the destination buffer's size is known and that the count argument used in the buffer operation does not exceed this size. If the destination is a pointer, pass the buffer size as an additional argument to the function and use it to limit the copy operation. For example, if the vulnerable code is:\n\n```cpp\n// Vulnerable: destination size is unknown\nstrncpy(dst, src, count);\n```\n\nA safe approach is:\n\n```cpp\n// Assume 'dst' is a char pointer and 'dst_size' is the size of the buffer\nstrncpy(dst, src, dst_size - 1);\ndst[dst_size - 1] = '\\0'; // Ensure null-termination\n```\n\nAlways validate that the count does not exceed the destination buffer's capacity to prevent buffer overflows.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-131: Incorrect Calculation of Buffer Size](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/131.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\n___\n"
