              "id": "85e89344-81e0-4d8f-994e-98800b02fb30",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as high risk because the destination buffer's capacity is not known at the point of the buffer operation, and the count or length argument used in the operation is not proven to be safe. This means there is a significant risk of a buffer overflow if the count exceeds the actual size of the destination buffer. The lack of information about the destination buffer's size and the absence of explicit safety checks make this a genuine vulnerability. No evidence of safety mechanisms, such as bounds checks or capacity derivation, is present in the available data.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo remediate this issue, ensure that the count or length argument used in the buffer operation does not exceed the actual size of the destination buffer. Before performing the operation, explicitly check the size of the destination buffer and limit the count accordingly. For example, if you have a destination buffer and a count parameter, you can add a check like this:\n\n```cpp\nif (count > DEST_BUFFER_SIZE) {\n    // Handle error: count exceeds buffer size\n    return ERROR_CODE;\n}\n// Safe to proceed with the buffer operation\n```\n\nReplace `DEST_BUFFER_SIZE` with the actual size of your destination buffer. This prevents writing beyond the buffer's bounds and mitigates the risk of buffer overflow.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [CWE-120: Buffer Copy without Checking Size of Input ('Classic Buffer Overflow')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/120.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-131: Incorrect Calculation of Buffer Size](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/131.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
